CAT = "sgm5Aml"; SEG = "AML"
Q = [
('Which MAS notice sets anti-money laundering and countering the financing of terrorism duties for financial advisers?',
 'FAA-N06', ['FAA-N16', 'FAA-N20', 'FAA-N26'],
 'FAA-N06 covers risk assessment, customer due diligence, record keeping, suspicious transaction reporting and internal controls for financial advisers.'),
('Under FAA-N06, a financial adviser may open an account in a fictitious name:',
 'Never', ['If the client is a VIP', 'With senior management approval', 'For accounts below a set size'],
 'FAA-N06 states that no financial adviser shall open or maintain an anonymous account or an account in a fictitious name.'),
('Customer due diligence is required when the adviser establishes business relations, when it doubts earlier information, and when:',
 'Laundering is suspected', ['The client changes jobs', 'The client turns 65', 'A policy anniversary arrives'],
 'FAA-N06 requires CDD on establishing business relations, on any suspicion of money laundering or terrorism financing, and when the adviser doubts the veracity or adequacy of earlier information.'),
('Which detail must be obtained to identify an individual customer?',
 'Residential address', ['Monthly salary', "Employer's name", 'Religious affiliation'],
 'FAA-N06 lists full name including aliases, unique identification number, residential address, date of birth and nationality.'),
('Before establishing business relations, the adviser has reasonable grounds to suspect the funds are criminal proceeds. It must:',
 'Not proceed and file an STR', ['Proceed but monitor closely', 'Ask the client to explain later', 'Refer him to another adviser'],
 'FAA-N06 says the adviser shall not establish business relations or undertake the transaction, and shall file a suspicious transaction report.'),
('Suspicious transaction reports are filed with:',
 'STRO', ['The Singapore Exchange', 'The Life Insurance Association', 'The CPF Board'],
 'Reports go to the Suspicious Transaction Reporting Office (STRO) of the Commercial Affairs Department of the Singapore Police Force, with a copy to MAS on request.'),
('A suspicious transaction should be reported:',
 'Regardless of the amount', ['Only above a set amount', 'Only if completed', "Only after a year's monitoring"],
 'FAA-N06 requires prompt reports on suspicious transactions, including attempted transactions, regardless of the amount.'),
('Which Singapore law makes it an offence to tip off a person about a suspicious transaction report?',
 'The CDSA', ['The Financial Advisers Act', 'The Companies Act', 'The Insurance Act'],
 'Section 57 of the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act (CDSA) makes tipping off an offence. FAA-N06 reminds advisers of it.'),
('The adviser suspects money laundering and believes carrying out further CDD would alert the client. It may:',
 'Stop the CDD and file an STR', ['Carry on and warn the client', 'Close the file with no report', 'Ask the client to find another adviser'],
 'FAA-N06 lets the adviser stop the CDD measures where they would tip off the customer, document why, and file an STR.'),
('When a customer is a politically exposed person, the adviser must at least get senior management approval, enhanced monitoring and:',
 'Source of wealth and funds', ['A guarantee from his employer', 'Approval from MAS', 'A cash deposit'],
 'FAA-N06 requires senior management approval, reasonable steps to establish source of wealth and source of funds, and enhanced ongoing monitoring for PEPs.'),
('FAA-N06 requires transaction records to be kept in a way that lets each transaction be:',
 'Reconstructed if needed', ["Reversed on the client's demand", 'Shown to other clients', 'Deleted after the next audit'],
 'Records must allow any transaction to be reconstructed, including amount and currency, to provide evidence if needed. They are kept for at least 5 years after the transaction is completed.'),
('If an adviser cannot complete the required CDD measures for a new customer, it must:',
 'Not start the business relationship', ['Start it and finish CDD later', 'Ask the client for a larger premium', "Get the client's verbal promise"],
 'FAA-N06 says an adviser unable to complete CDD shall not commence or continue business relations, and shall consider filing an STR.'),
('FAA-N06 requires a financial adviser to appoint an AML/CFT compliance officer at:',
 'Management level', ['Any staff level', 'Representative level', 'The product issuer'],
 'The AML/CFT compliance officer must be at management level, suitably qualified, adequately resourced and have timely access to customer records.'),
('Simplified CDD may NOT be used where the customer is from:',
 'A FATF countermeasure country', ['Singapore', 'A low-risk listed company', 'A government department'],
 'FAA-N06 bars simplified CDD for customers from a country for which the FATF has called for countermeasures, or known to have inadequate AML/CFT measures.'),
('Before launching a new product or delivery channel, a financial adviser must:',
 'Assess its ML/TF risks', ["Get every client's consent", 'Lower its CDD standards', 'Notify the police'],
 'FAA-N06 requires the adviser to assess money laundering and terrorism financing risks of new products, practices and technologies before launch, paying special attention to those that favour anonymity.'),
("A Singapore financial adviser's overseas branch faces weaker local AML rules. Under FAA-N06 the branch should apply:",
 'The higher standard', ["Only the host country's rules", 'Whichever is cheaper', 'No AML rules at all'],
 "FAA-N06 requires overseas branches and subsidiaries to apply the higher of Singapore's and the host country's AML/CFT standards, as far as host law permits."),
]
